# Implementation Plan - Veritas Two-Step Local AI Search Ingestion

This plan outlines the implementation of a two-step Local AI process in the Veritas dashboard. We will enable live querying of Anakin's Wire API, classify queries using a local LLM, fetch data in parallel, and generate the final executive summary.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Architecture Decisions:**
> 1. **Local LLM Settings & Fallbacks:** The app expects Ollama to be running locally at `http://localhost:11434`. If Ollama is not active or fails to classify, we will fall back to a rule-based heuristic classification and use standard template content (or Gemini, if configured) to ensure the system remains resilient.
> 2. **Anakin Wire API Integration:** We will execute `Promise.all` requests to `https://api.anakin.io/v1/wire/task` using the `X-API-Key` configured by the user. If the key is missing or the requests fail, we fall back to generating highly realistic mock data for the requested query.
> 3. **Developer Settings Expansion:** We will add a new field to the "Developer Settings" drawer to store the "Anakin Wire API Key" securely in local storage.

